>: Listen closely to decode vintage audio tapes and complete the transcriptions.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Text Quiz</strong>: Answer riddles to improve phone screen quality and track down who rented the movie.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <strong>Star Drag-and-Drop</strong>: Align the Little Dipper star pattern to reveal the first lyrics of <i>Walk Alone</i>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4389350/extras/ded6205ce444181e081c9de0a71e5530.avif?t=1782463330\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4389350/extras_big/ded6205ce444181e081c9de0a71e5530.avif?t=1782463330 width=1560 height=438 /></span></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4389350/extras/f1ed76fc6237a0894627333e796ad16a.webp?t=1782463330\" width=800 height=18 /></span>💬  <strong>ENGLISH WITH AN ITALIAN FLAVOUR</strong><br>Designed for a global audience, but keeping the authentic spirit of a summer abroad, the interface and core dialogue are in English. However, to stay true to the characters' roots, some exchanges between the Italian protagonists remain in their native tongue—always translated or rephrased within the narrative. For a deeper dive, entire key segments of the game can be experienced in both English and Italian, offering a fluid, multicultural journey that captures the authentic spirit of a summer abroad.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4389350/extras/7488109a4b52172547dd78d90b9567ed.avif?t=1782463330\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4389350/extras_big/7488109a4b52172547dd78d90b9567ed.avif?t=1782463330 width=1560 height=450 /></span></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4389350/extras/c13148c6e6caaf981c164a2caac67909.avif?t=1782463330\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4389350/extras_big/c13148c6e6caaf981c164a2caac67909.avif?t=1782463330 width=1560 height=450 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "short_description": "Three teenagers find a mysterious audio tape recording which turns out to be evidence of a murder. It’s the end of the world as they know it. Immerse yourself in a kinetic novel that encapsulates the essence of the 1990s by completely reinventing its music scene.", "supported_languages": "English", "reviews": "“The exact opposite of corporate AI logic.”<br>Il Venerdì di Repubblica<br><br>“If you’re a visual novel fan, this gem of a game is begging you to play it and become immersed in its world.”<br>8.5 / 10  – The Gaming Outsider<br><br>“The game from Gaigo Studio is a rare find. An interactive comic that knows exactly what it wants to be and completely ignores traditional gaming labels. It is an experience for those who love well-told stories, one that doesn't shout or scramble in an attempt to become pop.”<br>3.5/5 – GameCvlt<br>", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4389350/c1c2c2e66eb7d1a71efc5e22d981e1f474341eb5/header.jpg?t=1782463330", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4389350/1eea8de61b2c57a0d0ae9f07a6055f436d09df50/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1782463330", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4389350/1eea8de61b2c57a0d0ae9f07a6055f436d09df50/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1782463330", "website": null, "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS:</stro